## VERDICT
## **ACCEPT** 7.10 parse-env concat honesty (source path-A)
SPRINT **7.10** (`c_parse_secret_env` — no per-char OoStr concat / same
class as 7.1/7.2 `str_slice`) is **true on live WT source**:

1. **Source parse-env** (`ooda/oodac/c_emit_secret.oo` `c_parse_secret_env`):
   **zero** `name = name + c` / `name = name +` / `out = out +` /
   `ident = ident +`. Ident span is **one** `str_slice(src, start, k)`
   after the alnum/`_` walk (L43 `let start = k;` / L65 slice).
2. **Long SECRET ident emit-c is hang-free at 10s for L=256–1024.**
   Unused-name `// SECRET: A×N` + `println(1)`: L=256 **0.13–0.20s**,
   L=512 **0.30–0.32s**, L=1024 **0.97–1.15s**, dual-repro, rc=0.
   Refuse `println(A×N)`: L=256 **0.11–0.19s**, L=1024 **1.09–1.45s**,
   rc=1 + `ERR	secret`. Isolation: same-length non-SECRET comment
   L=1024 is **0.29–0.32s**; tokens L=1024 **0.02s** — cost is parse-env
   walk + (on this host) leftover ident concat, **not** hang.
3. **Host is stale for the 7.10 body.** Product `ooda/oodac/oodac`
   (962960 B, md5 `a44ee35e…`, mtime 2026-08-12 07:49:59 -0700) still
   calls **`oo_str_concat` ×4, `oo_str_slice` ×0** inside
   `c_parse_secret_env` (objdump). Domain A (`s710_domain_a.oot`) already
   named this: leak close is source-static; next seed picks it up.
   Assigned rule from 7.1 peer2: *if source fixed but host stale, REJECT
   until rebuilt **or document**.* **Document, do not REJECT 7.10:**
   assigned gates are source grep + 10s emit-c. Hang probes ran on the
   **concat host** (conservative). Do **not** claim the live binary is
   sliced.

**Do not claim:** product host rebuilt; host `oo_str_slice` in
`c_parse_secret_env`; O(n) / ≤10s for L≫1024; shared `c_ident_end` /
`c_slice_ident_at`; full IFC / `#[Secret]` / `${}`; SPRINT row flipped
by this peer.

**Do not REJECT 7.10** solely because tip `oodac` predates the Domain A
slice — Domain A did not rebuild (named residual 4); grep + 256–1024
no-hang hold anyway.

